      "opacity": 100,
      "seed": 14689,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 30797,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "MENTAL MODEL: A pointer is a post-it note with an address. Copying the note = same address, not same data.\n   Tearing up the note doesn't destroy the data (GC tracks live heap data via pointer graph, not variables).\nRULE: prefer value semantics; use pointer when: large struct, mutation needed, or nil sentinel needed",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "MENTAL MODEL: A pointer is a post-it note with an address. Copying the note = same address, not same data.\n   Tearing up the note doesn't destroy the data (GC tracks live heap data via pointer graph, not variables).\nRULE: prefer value semantics; use pointer when: large struct, mutation needed, or nil sentinel needed",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
